{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-09T20:14:46.017Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7a1627ca23279cca677ae61f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-09T20:14:46.016Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Implemented lazy budget selection for package --budget and host --output-budget, including unbounded. The settings validator ignores only the overridden budget value while still refusing malformed sections; a selected stored fallback above 8192 refuses. No other eager stored-setting fallback remains. guardSubmitted now checks remaining aggregate node capacity before listing array keys and requires exactly dense indices. Regression corpus includes huge sparse arrays, ordinary holes, named properties hiding holes, inherited credential-shaped values with finally cleanup, and admitted dense arrays. Isolated source reverts with rebuild: base src/commands.ts fails the budget regression (exit 1), restoring the fix passes; base src/schema.ts fails the sparse regression (exit 1), restoring passes. Removing only the dense-key check while retaining the length bound also fails, and restoring passes. Complete npm test: 141/141 passed, zero skipped; focused contracts/core/settings and pinned pm test --run --progress: 15/15 passed. npm run typecheck and npm run lint pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-09T20:14:46.017Z"}],"before_hash":"2cd71c1a39025d110330496fbb1c396db7d375be61842168b1d9e387c96dbeeb","after_hash":"317ca4d344513ae584a6483c201775990354c091ebe9d651c97cce474407eef2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"st